# MVVM and UI

Full spec: `docs/wiki/Coding-Standards.md`.

- Every view has a ViewModel in `Unison.Core/ViewModels`. Bind `DataContext`; commands are `RelayCommand`.
- Collection items with actions (`ChatMessage`, chat rows) are ViewModels created by DI factories — never `new` from a view.
- Bindings and Behaviors (`Microsoft.Xaml.Interactivity`) for actions. Code-behind only: navigation, Loaded/Unloaded, Storyboards, `MediaElement`, scroll.
- Reusable visuals → `UI/Controls/`. Dialogs → `UI/Dialogs/` shown only via `IDialogService` (pass the target VM when the dialog has form state).
- Converters → `UI/Converters/`. Templates → `UI/Templates/`. No ViewModels in UWP.
- Strings: `x:Uid` / `IStringResources` / `.resw` in all shipped languages. No hardcoded UI copy in a VM.
- Routes in `NavigationRoutes`; page types only in `NavigatorService`.

Exceptions (do not “fix” in passing): `ChatDetailView` list/scroll/MediaElement; `VisibleChats` safe-mode mirror. Move slices toward the VM, do not expand the hybrid.
